            <ArticleTitle>[Recurrent ventricular fibrillation in a patient with Prinzmetal angina pectoris--case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>177-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The description of the case of 35 years old patient with paroxysmal ventricular fibrillation in a course of Prinzmetal angina pectoris treated unsuccessfully with antiarrhythmic drugs who required implantation of cardioverter/defibrillator. The via-venous cardioverter/defibrillator was implanted (ICD). During 6 months observation ventricular tachycardia and ventricular fibrillation occurred four times and was effectively interrupted by the cardioverter/defibrillator.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
